From 14951ddb08983cd433fae87fb8c1b3f827f24f0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangGuoDong <zhangguodong@kylinos.cn>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:13:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 00/21] smb/server: refactor smb2_open()

smb2_open() was already long, and it has grown much larger over the
past few months. This makes the code harder to read and change.
Many memory leaks and reference leaks have already been found in
this function.

This patchset reduces smb2_open() from 1336 lines to 720 lines.
And I plan to keep refactoring smb2_open() to make it shorter.

No functional change is intended.

ZhangGuoDong (21):
  smb/server: add struct smb2_create_contexts
  smb/server: factor out smb2_parse_posix_context()
  smb/server: factor out smb2_parse_create_contexts()
  smb/server: factor out smb2_apply_create_contexts()
  smb/server: factor out smb2_open_oplock()
  smb/server: factor out smb2_check_create_request()
  smb/server: factor out smb2_query_maximal_access()
  smb/server: factor out smb2_init_create_acl()
  smb/server: factor out smb2_get_create_name()
  smb/server: factor out smb2_parse_lease_context()
  smb/server: track CREATE contexts with last_context in smb2_open()
  smb/server: replace contxt_cnt with last_context in smb2_open()
  smb/server: calculate CREATE response iov_len once in smb2_open()
  smb/server: factor out smb2_add_create_context() and use it for AAPL
  smb/server: use smb2_add_create_context() for POSIX responses
  smb/server: use smb2_add_create_context() for durable v2 responses
  smb/server: use smb2_add_create_context() for durable v1 responses
  smb/server: use smb2_add_create_context() for disk ID responses
  smb/server: use smb2_add_create_context() for maximal access responses
  smb/server: use smb2_add_create_context() for lease responses
  smb/server: factor out smb2_build_create_rsp()

 fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c | 1557 ++++++++++++++++++++-------------------
 1 file changed, 790 insertions(+), 767 deletions(-)

